########## what the pane proves / does not prove ##########
PROVES: PROVES: the REAL dsh-tui host boots in the sandbox, mounts this wave's bundle, opens /settings and RENDERS the `MPD 插件包 (mpd)` section — header, the 22-field declaration and the nine team-model slot rows with their resolved values.
PROVES: PROVES: the section is not empty/degraded (it is page 1 of 42 of the plugin-settings screen) and the nine slot rows are individually VISIBLE at this geometry (they are the last nine rows of the section).
PROVES: PROVES: the assertion engine is falsifiable — the script's own negative control on the same captured panes is red by design (control.ok=false).
DOES NOT PROVE: NOT proven: that a user CLICKED/OPENED a slot picker — no key was sent to a slot row; the case's pattern set does not isolate the slot rows, and its single ok=false is caused by the unreachable /never lost/ pattern, so the case's own boolean is not usable as the wave's proof.
DOES NOT PROVE: NOT proven: the full disclosure text is legible on screen — the hint is truncated at this geometry (offset 320 > 170-char cut), so the never-lost clause is composed but not visible.
DOES NOT PROVE: NOT proven: anything about the WEB card (that is t9's evidence) or about member ROUTING (t10/t12).
DOES NOT PROVE: Scope note: extending the case to isolate the slot rows would edit skills/** and force a VENDOR_LOCK re-pin, which this wave deliberately avoids — so the case was run as-is.

